      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Conformal field theory gave an enduring, highly predictive account of two-dimensional criticality and profoundly reshaped statistical physics.",
        "attribution": "Polyakov, Zamolodchikov, and Cardy made distinct foundational contributions to the framework and its physical use.",
        "maturity": "Its consequences have been tested and used across critical phenomena for many decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
