        "Andrea J. Liu",
        "Sidney R. Nagel",
        "Corey S. O'Hern"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The jamming transition revealed a clean organizing principle for rigidity, disorder, and emergent mechanical response in many-particle matter.",
        "attribution": "Liu and Nagel articulated the central jamming perspective, while O'Hern supplied decisive numerical formulation and evidence.",
        "maturity": "The framework has generated sustained theory, simulation, and experimental work across soft matter.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Whether jamming has sufficient universality across real, driven materials remains an active question."
        ]
      }
    },
